<p align="center">&nbsp;

<p align="center"><font size="4" face="Helvetica,arial">SOLUSEK
RO BRANCH<br>
ENCHANTED CIRCLE GUILD EVENTS</font><p align="center"><font face="Helvetica,arial" size="2">The
next scheduled guild event is for February the 25th at 2 p.m. (this is a Sunday)
Pacific Standard Time.&nbsp; The event will be held in and around the Runnyeye
Dungeon.&nbsp; Information for this event shall be posted to this page in the
very near future.</font><p align="center"><font face="Helvetica,arial" size="2">The
background is available for download immediately in Word format and RTF.&nbsp;
Both files are zipped for your convenience.</font><p align="center"><font face="Helvetica,arial">Word<br>
<a href="A%20Tale%20of%20Woe%20-word.zip">A Tale of Woe -word.zip</a></font><p align="center"><font face="Helvetica,arial">RTF<br>
<a href="A%20Tale%20of%20Woe%20-rtf.zip">A Tale of Woe -rtf.zip</a></font>
<p align="center"><font face="Helvetica,arial"><b>GUILD EVENT PRELIMINARY
INFORMATION</b></font>
<div>
  &nbsp;
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2">/OOC Read &quot;A Tale of Woe&quot; before reading
  the information below or it will not make sense.</font>
  <p><font face="Arial" size="2"><b>A note found at the guild hall from Erik
  Torvald:</b></font>
</div>
<div>
  <b>&nbsp;</b>
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2"><b>&quot;My comrades.&nbsp; Through fault of mine
  the Guild Leader has been taken by the Evil Eyes of Runnyeye.&nbsp; I take all
  blame for this and will accept any punishment deemed necessary by the Guild as
  seen fit to administer.&nbsp; As instructed by Commander Renain I am leaving
  detailed instructions on how to find the lair of those most vile as to take
  our Liege Lord.</b></font>
</div>
<div>
  <b>&nbsp;</b>
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2"><b>From the Guild Hall turn right and head up the
  Gorge until you reach The Gorge of King Xorbb.&nbsp; Once at the gorge stay to
  the right mountain side and you shall then attain&nbsp; the goal of Runnyeye
  Citadel.&nbsp; Within you shall discover the Evil Eyes and their Knoll
  minions.</b></font>
</div>
<div>
  <b>&nbsp;</b>
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2"><b>I am rushing to catch Nuuan, Banehawk and
  Renain to aid them in the attempt to retrieve Hablur.&nbsp; Should we fail you
  are the only hope to save Hablur and avenge our deaths.&nbsp;</b></font>
</div>
<div>
  <b>&nbsp;</b>
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2"><b>With much regret,</b></font>
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2"><b>Guardsmen Erik Torvald&quot;</b></font>
</div>
<div>
  &nbsp;
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2">/OOC</font>
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2">The Guild event will begin at the set of building
  closest to the Gorge Zone.&nbsp; The highest ranking officer is responsible
  for gathering everyone in that area and heading out to the Gorge Zone at 2pm
  PST.&nbsp; If you are late try to catch up.&nbsp; When the group gets to the
  Zone line at the Gorge they are to wait until Eriktorvald says to zone into
  the Gorge Zone.&nbsp; I strongly suggest being buffed as much as possible at
  this point.&nbsp; Once across you will be given instructions by the Guard
  Commander and the Defender Commander.&nbsp; They are ultimately responsible
  for leading the group at this point.</font>
</div>
<div>
  &nbsp;
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2">This is a massive role play event and is meant for
  the levels 20+ with an emphasis on the higher level people 30+.&nbsp; If you
  are below 30 I caution you that despite the massive firepower we will have
  their that it is possible for deaths to occur for the lower level people.&nbsp;
  You are more than welcome but I must caution you.&nbsp; It is highly doubtful
  if we have a good showing of our higher level members anyone will die but
  follow their lead and you will be ok.</font>
</div>
<div>
  &nbsp;
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2">During the time we are in the event only use Guild
  Chat.&nbsp; If anyone knows any higher level Clerics, Shamans or Druids from
  other guilds they are welcome to join us.&nbsp; To be truthful anyone is
  allowed to join but having healing classes will help save people.&nbsp; I ask
  that all higher levels form groups with the lower levels to keep an eye on
  their hit points so if they need help it can be quickly rendered.&nbsp;
  Depending on the number of people we have in the event please try not to chat
  too much or it will make it very confusing.&nbsp; This is a massive event with
  the guild and it will put strain on each group to maintain communications with
  the other groups.&nbsp; The group leader of each group should be the one
  focusing attacks etc.&nbsp; Think of each minigroup as having a squad leader
  and those in the group follow his orders.&nbsp; This will greatly help prevent
  confusion.</font>
</div>
<div>
  &nbsp;
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2">Those of you that have VC should use it.&nbsp;
  This will greatly help each unit leader coordinate things.&nbsp;</font>
</div>
<div>
  &nbsp;
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2">This dungeon is NOT dangerous to those 30+ but can
  be dangerous if people don't work as a team.&nbsp; None of the higher levels
  should have any troubles but I strongly recommend taking each step slow and
  careful.&nbsp; This is a dungeon crawl.</font>
</div>
<div>
  &nbsp;
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2">At any point in this adventure someone may receive
  a duel message.&nbsp; This will be done by lotto on my part.&nbsp; In fact if
  the duelist is defeated the lotto process will continue until the challenger
  has been defeated.&nbsp; I am being vague to make this part exciting.</font>
</div>
<div>
  &nbsp;
</div>
<div>
  <font face="Arial" size="2">The higher levels that will be there are:&nbsp;
  Nuuan, Mujahid, Renain, Einlain, Maliik, Verticaly, Ceaorn, Aelron for sure
  (as far as I know).&nbsp; That is 8 people 39+.&nbsp; There are a lot of mid
  levels like Banehawk, Zuggar, Corvas, etc that will be there.&nbsp; To
  alleviate fears Hablur has gone thru the entire dungeon by himself and had
  zero problems.&nbsp; The only thing I fear is Nuuan losing his pet and it
  running off killing everything in the dungeon before everyone can help :)</font>
</div>
